#let who = "world"
#let greet = (name) => "Hello, " + name

Value splice: #who and a call chain: #greet("tsm").
Member access: #who.length characters; expression: #(1 + 2 * 3).
#{ let hidden = 40 + 2 }Statement splice binds in document scope: #hidden.
A splice ends at punctuation: #who. Semicolon terminator: #who;[not an argument].
Content argument desugars to a trailing argument: #strong[bold text].
Literal hash: \#who stays literal.
